<section class="section" id="architecture"><div class="site-container"><div class="section-heading"><div><div class="section-kicker">Architecture</div><h2>Same core.<br/>Same agent.</h2></div><p>The surface changes. The foundation does not: terminal, ACP, and headless converge on <code>cetas-core</code>, then Posoco and the configured model provider.</p></div><div class="architecture-stage"><div class="architecture-flow"><div class="arch-surfaces"><div class="arch-node"><strong>Terminal</strong><span>cetas-js</span></div><div class="arch-node"><strong>Editor / ACP</strong><span>cetas-acp</span></div><div class="arch-node"><strong>Headless</strong><span>cetas-headless</span></div></div><div class="arch-arrow">→</div><div class="arch-core"><strong>cetas-core</strong><span>shared assembly</span></div><div class="arch-arrow">→</div><div class="arch-core"><strong>Posoco</strong><span>agent → provider</span></div></div><div class="arch-note"><span><strong>Different surfaces, one product identity.</strong> The website mirrors how the repository is assembled today.</span><a class="text-link" href="/docs/architecture/">Read the architecture →</a></div></div></div></section>